// Regression: hotkey starvation under interval load (high-priority hotkeys).
// The yield pump's stale-suspension poison made a hotkey goroutine picked
// after a busy sibling's dispatch consume zero instructions (the fast
// path's first-opcode guard saw the leftover last_suspension_reason_) and
// park it with reason None and no wake path, so hotkeys never fired while
// any interval/poll loop ran. Fixed: the consumed reason is cleared after
// each dispatch outcome, and a not-really-suspended fiber is requeued
// instead of being bricked.
// Expected: fired==1 within 1s of trigger; rc 0. Headless-safe: F24 is a
// persistent goroutine fired via hotkey.trigger (no OS input needed).
fired = 0
F24 => {
    fired = fired + 1
}

ticks = 0
iv = interval 5 {
    i = 0
    while i < 400000 {
        i = i + 1
    }
    ticks = ticks + 1
}

sleep(300)
t0 = time.millis()
hotkey.trigger("F24")
while fired == 0 && time.millis() - t0 < 1000 {
    sleep(5)
}
print("fired:", fired, " latency_ms:", time.millis() - t0, " ticks:", ticks)
if fired != 1 {
    print("FAIL hk-starvation-interval: hotkey never fired under load")
    process.exit(255)
}
process.exit(0)
